1
00:00:00,112 --> 00:00:01,312
Time is a quiet thief.

2
00:00:01,725 --> 00:00:03,887
It doesn't steal a legacy all at once.

3
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:04,950
It erodes it,

4
00:00:05,188 --> 00:00:06,062
season by season.

5
00:00:06,550 --> 00:00:08,438
First the laughter from the grand halls,

6
00:00:08,712 --> 00:00:10,025
then the warmth from the hearth,

7
00:00:10,325 --> 00:00:12,138
and finally the roof that was built to

8
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:13,513
protect those memories.

9
00:00:13,912 --> 00:00:14,737
Look at this place.

10
00:00:15,150 --> 00:00:16,875
It is not just an abandoned mansion.

11
00:00:17,288 --> 00:00:19,175
It is a monument to impermanence.

12
00:00:19,588 --> 00:00:21,562
Ivy has crawled up the stone facade,

13
00:00:21,838 --> 00:00:23,212
claiming it back for the earth.

14
00:00:23,625 --> 00:00:24,550
Nature is patient.

15
00:00:24,962 --> 00:00:26,250
It waits for us to leave,

16
00:00:26,625 --> 00:00:28,825
and then it quietly erases our footsteps.

17
00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:31,938
The glass of the grand conservatory lies shattered

18
00:00:31,950 --> 00:00:33,838
in the dust like crushed diamonds.

19
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:36,725
Floorboards once polished to a mirror finish are

20
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:39,162
buckled and warped by decades of rain.

21
00:00:39,588 --> 00:00:42,550
The grand staircase curves upward into nothing but

22
00:00:42,562 --> 00:00:45,100
collapsed ceilings and empty doorways.

23
00:00:45,512 --> 00:00:47,975
And yet, beneath the wind howling through the

24
00:00:47,988 --> 00:00:50,912
broken rafters, the bones of this house are

25
00:00:50,925 --> 00:00:51,762
still strong.

26
00:00:52,175 --> 00:00:53,650
It is not waiting for a miracle.

27
00:00:54,062 --> 00:00:55,500
It is waiting for an intervention.

28
00:00:55,912 --> 00:00:57,100
So let's rewind the clock.
